WEBVTT

00:07.507 --> 00:12.267
<b>The Steppe, Ever Unchanging</b>

00:12.657 --> 00:13.457
What?

00:14.177 --> 00:16.997
Princess Sorghaghtani 
refused the marriage?

00:16.997 --> 00:18.547
Yeah, it's a surprise—

00:18.547 --> 00:20.207
What'll become of Lady Töregene?

00:20.207 --> 00:23.877
Lady Töregene's freedom was contingent 
on the princess marrying!

00:23.877 --> 00:25.327
What did Empress Boraqchin say?

00:25.327 --> 00:26.587
Calm down.

00:26.587 --> 00:28.277
I'll tell you everything.

00:31.457 --> 00:33.137
Sorghaghtani Beki.

00:33.897 --> 00:38.327
This is what is best for the Mongols,
and it will benefit you as well.

00:39.317 --> 00:42.057
Humbly accept this offer
we extend to you.

00:44.657 --> 00:46.777
I deeply appreciate your courtesy.

00:47.577 --> 00:53.937
However, our great foremother, Alan Gua,
once said to her five sons:

00:54.397 --> 00:56.807
"A single arrow may be broken with ease,

00:56.807 --> 00:59.667
but five arrows bundled together
 shan't ever be broken."

01:00.477 --> 01:01.747
Great Kha'an.

01:01.747 --> 01:04.737
Tolui was one of the arrows at your side.

01:05.437 --> 01:07.557
It falls upon me to raise his sons.

01:07.937 --> 01:11.197
They are still young and fragile
 arrows in the making.

01:13.467 --> 01:15.387
The House of Tolui stands on its own?

01:15.757 --> 01:18.757
She won't let it be engulfed 
by the House of Ögedei?

01:19.987 --> 01:22.797
And I'm sure your retainers
 feel the same way.

01:23.437 --> 01:25.067
Isn't that right, General Ilüge?

01:25.067 --> 01:26.677
Huh? Uh, yes.

01:26.677 --> 01:29.487
You are the head retainer 
serving the House of Ögedei.

01:29.487 --> 01:32.947
I imagine the Great Kha'an 
will entrust you with his finest treasure,

01:33.177 --> 01:35.537
as a sign of his utmost confidence in you.

01:37.537 --> 01:39.167
Treasure?

01:39.167 --> 01:41.487
You mean to say Lady Töregene is...

01:41.487 --> 01:42.417
Yeah.

01:42.787 --> 01:44.717
She's in General Ilüge's territory.

01:55.907 --> 01:58.597
<b>Jaadugar</b>

03:19.137 --> 03:21.167
You seem to be in a foul temper.

03:23.377 --> 03:26.857
Sorghaghtani sent over
 a messenger this morning.

03:26.457 --> 03:38.847
<b>House of Jochi</b>

03:26.457 --> 03:38.847
<b>House of Ögedei</b>

03:26.457 --> 03:38.847
<b>House of Chagatai</b>

03:26.457 --> 03:35.387
<b>House of Tolui</b>

03:26.457 --> 03:35.387
<b>House of Temüge</b>

03:27.757 --> 03:29.527
If the Great Kha'an so wishes,

03:29.527 --> 03:34.157
she's willing to offer up 4,000 tents
 from the House of Tolui.

03:34.627 --> 03:38.907
The territory and people I had planned 
to deprive of her all along.

03:40.787 --> 03:42.417
She's making a mockery of me.

03:44.817 --> 03:47.487
Are you angry at me for what I've done?

03:48.347 --> 03:50.377
Why should I condemn you?

03:50.827 --> 03:54.277
I am finally able to do what I set out to.

03:54.797 --> 03:56.097
It's all thanks to you.

03:58.457 --> 03:59.857
However, I must say this.

04:00.837 --> 04:04.287
Please don't involve Töregene any longer.

04:05.177 --> 04:08.107
She is someone who is special to me.

04:10.587 --> 04:11.967
I understand.

04:13.527 --> 04:16.657
Prince Güyük and Sir Qadaq are heading
to General Ilüge's territory as we speak.

04:17.407 --> 04:20.917
General Ilüge served as 
the Great Kha'an's tutor for many years.

04:21.287 --> 04:24.077
His influence rivals that 
of the imperial family itself.

04:24.437 --> 04:28.997
Not even Prince Güyük can intrude 
upon his land without good reason.

04:29.227 --> 04:30.937
Shira, let's hurry.

04:31.357 --> 04:33.337
Be sure to hold on tight.

04:33.647 --> 04:34.797
Thanks.

04:36.527 --> 04:38.437
We've got a rough road ahead of us.

04:50.737 --> 04:52.187
Excuse me, Lady Töregene—

04:55.227 --> 04:57.577
Have you mistaken me 
for that problem child again?

04:57.577 --> 04:59.727
M-My apologies!

05:03.027 --> 05:06.027
There are too many tents 
for me to remember.

05:09.067 --> 05:11.247
Why, if it isn't Prince Güyük.

05:11.487 --> 05:13.667
What brings you to my home?

05:15.637 --> 05:18.207
Lady Töregene is here, isn't she?

05:18.207 --> 05:19.797
We'd like to speak with her.

05:19.797 --> 05:22.387
I'm afraid I don't know what you mean.

05:23.457 --> 05:27.627
Don't think we've come all this way
purely based on wild conjecture.

05:28.177 --> 05:31.357
It's a long story, 
but let me tell you all about it.

05:36.647 --> 05:42.067
They told us to make sure she's safe 
while they have him distracted.

05:42.647 --> 05:44.177
But how do we even find her?

05:44.177 --> 05:47.317
Forget about success. 
If we're found, it could mean our heads.

05:47.317 --> 05:48.807
H-Hey, Fatima!

05:51.667 --> 05:52.487
This way.

05:53.667 --> 05:55.547
This could mean trouble.

05:55.857 --> 05:59.927
We must do everything we can to conceal 
the fact that Lady Töregene is here.

06:06.837 --> 06:08.227
What's wrong? Let's go.

06:08.857 --> 06:09.477
Right.

06:10.427 --> 06:12.117
And how is Lady Töregene?

06:12.427 --> 06:14.107
I went to see her just earlier...

06:18.437 --> 06:19.877
Did you hear that?

06:19.877 --> 06:23.457
We've confirmed she's safe, 
so let's go back for now—

06:23.457 --> 06:24.987
Hey!

06:33.477 --> 06:37.257
Lady Töregene, thanks for waiting. 
I've brought your meal.

06:38.447 --> 06:39.547
You're late.

06:39.777 --> 06:42.477
My apologies. I got lost again.

06:49.657 --> 06:50.937
No urum?

06:51.987 --> 06:54.817
The season for urum has long passed.

06:55.367 --> 06:56.737
I was just asking.

06:57.357 --> 06:58.447
Now, leave me.

06:58.447 --> 06:59.777
O-Of course.

07:13.547 --> 07:14.677
Fatima.

07:15.977 --> 07:17.547
<i>Lady Töregene.</i>

07:17.937 --> 07:19.237
<i>Lady Töregene.</i>

07:20.387 --> 07:21.367
<i>Lady Töregene!</i>

07:21.367 --> 07:23.577
Hey, wait. Let's head back.

07:25.257 --> 07:28.217
Lady Töregene's so hard to please.

07:51.457 --> 07:52.537
Lady Töregene!

07:52.767 --> 07:54.207
Fatima?

07:54.717 --> 07:56.147
Why are you here?

07:56.147 --> 07:58.587
I'm so glad to see you safe.

07:58.587 --> 08:00.337
We finally meet again.

08:04.047 --> 08:07.557
I betrayed you.

08:11.257 --> 08:13.457
Lady Töregene, look.

08:15.467 --> 08:17.667
You managed to protect them.

08:18.107 --> 08:22.817
The feelings most precious to me.

08:23.817 --> 08:24.597
No.

08:26.097 --> 08:28.057
To <i>us</i>.

08:32.477 --> 08:34.557
The Great Khatun said this to me:

08:36.337 --> 08:40.207
In the past, I waited upon Empress Khulan.

08:41.457 --> 08:42.207
Khulan?

08:43.217 --> 08:45.937
<i>The one who taught me 
to find joy in life.</i>

08:46.337 --> 08:51.007
<i>And who offered herself to the Mongols
for the Merkits facing ruin.</i>

08:51.007 --> 08:52.087
<i>Khulan.</i>

08:54.327 --> 08:57.367
I always sensed 
she bore feelings of resentment.

08:57.977 --> 09:02.397
To this day, you hide enmity
for the Mongols in your heart.

09:02.987 --> 09:04.197
Khulan did?

09:05.697 --> 09:08.277
Let me lend you my assistance.

09:10.717 --> 09:13.957
So that you can carry out her wishes.

09:15.397 --> 09:18.067
I thought my chance 
to finally kill Ögedei had come.

09:19.097 --> 09:23.167
The Great Khatun told me 
you weren't to be trusted.

09:26.287 --> 09:27.377
I was a fool.

09:28.157 --> 09:33.217
I fell for her lies 
and betrayed both you and Khulan.

09:36.387 --> 09:37.647
Lady Töregene.

09:39.057 --> 09:42.147
I found myself confronted as well.

09:43.847 --> 09:47.927
With the thought of abandoning the past 
and moving on with my life.

09:50.377 --> 09:53.087
I betrayed you.

09:54.867 --> 09:57.697
Fatima sure is taking her time talking.

09:58.227 --> 10:00.707
We should get going 
before we're discovered.

10:01.587 --> 10:04.447
W-Wait, are you serious?

10:04.447 --> 10:07.357
Sorry, but you're on your own
from here on out.

10:15.717 --> 10:16.737
I'm coming in.

10:19.517 --> 10:20.997
Great Kha'an.

10:24.717 --> 10:26.147
What do you want?

10:26.627 --> 10:30.027
If I'm to be executed, so be it.

10:30.027 --> 10:33.157
That's not it. I have a favor to ask.

10:34.857 --> 10:35.907
You may enter.

10:38.207 --> 10:40.287
M-Mother.

10:40.837 --> 10:42.097
My darling Güyük!

10:42.097 --> 10:43.337
<i>"My darling Güyük"?</i>

10:43.337 --> 10:46.687
Oh, what are <i>you</i> doing here, darling?

10:46.687 --> 10:48.167
Are you okay, darling?

10:48.167 --> 10:50.957
You didn't run into
 anything scary, did you?

10:49.497 --> 10:52.257
C-Calm down, Mother.

10:54.557 --> 10:58.407
Mother, please come to my territory.

10:59.147 --> 10:59.907
Huh?

11:00.337 --> 11:05.527
It lies to the west, on the steppe 
between the Altai Mountains and Tian Shan.

11:05.977 --> 11:10.507
The winters are cold, but there's plenty 
of water and the pastures are lush.

11:10.937 --> 11:12.037
And what's more...

11:13.297 --> 11:14.947
It's far from here.

11:19.317 --> 11:21.517
I ask you to go as well, Töregene.

11:22.327 --> 11:26.587
The court is much too tumultuous 
for you and Güyük, no?

11:27.627 --> 11:31.017
If you comply, I won't ask 
anything more of you.

11:33.337 --> 11:36.347
All I want is for you to be happy.

11:38.837 --> 11:40.247
<i>I see.</i>

11:40.247 --> 11:42.817
<i>That would resolve everything tidily.</i>

11:43.697 --> 11:48.387
<i>Empress Boraqchin wanted Prince Güyük 
and Princess Sorghaghtani to get married</i>

11:48.387 --> 11:50.857
<i>as a condition 
for Lady Töregene's freedom.</i>

11:51.557 --> 11:55.057
<i>Her aim was to remove the three of them 
from the imperial court.</i>

11:56.567 --> 11:59.327
<i>That particular scheme of hers 
didn't bear fruit.</i>

12:00.697 --> 12:05.707
<i>But this way, all three will leave
the political stage nonetheless.</i>

12:06.777 --> 12:10.337
<i>It's not a bad proposal 
for Lady Töregene, either.</i>

12:18.137 --> 12:19.717
Okay, Mother.

12:20.557 --> 12:23.217
I'll come fetch you tomorrow.

12:26.057 --> 12:27.767
Sorry to cause such a commotion.

12:28.237 --> 12:29.487
Will that be all?

12:29.487 --> 12:30.297
Yes.

12:31.537 --> 12:32.847
But before that...

12:34.807 --> 12:35.687
Töregene.

12:36.727 --> 12:39.527
Can I speak with 
your lady-in-waiting over there?

12:40.257 --> 12:41.077
Huh?

12:41.297 --> 12:41.927
Huh?

12:45.687 --> 12:47.327
Why me?

12:48.017 --> 12:49.937
So you're Fatima?

12:49.937 --> 12:51.367
Möge's told me about you.

12:51.367 --> 12:53.417
I hear you get lost easily.

12:55.877 --> 12:58.397
And it seems you're a scholar's daughter.

12:58.977 --> 13:00.597
Are you knowledgeable in the stars?

13:00.597 --> 13:01.967
The stars?

13:01.967 --> 13:03.727
P-Please, Great Kha'an!

13:03.727 --> 13:07.267
You mustn't speak directly 
to someone of such low class.

13:08.467 --> 13:10.677
Allow my son to relay your words.

13:10.677 --> 13:11.237
Go on.

13:11.237 --> 13:12.347
R-Right.

13:13.887 --> 13:17.097
The emperor asks, "Are you 
knowledgeable in the stars?"

13:17.097 --> 13:19.707
Why, yes. Considerably so.

13:21.777 --> 13:24.627
"Why, yes. Considerably so," she says.

13:24.627 --> 13:25.477
I see.

13:25.847 --> 13:29.127
Does she know why the stars 
move across the sky?

13:30.647 --> 13:35.517
"I see. Does she know why the stars 
move across the sky," he asks.

13:36.017 --> 13:37.447
Um...

13:37.767 --> 13:39.887
<i>Well, that much I </i>do<i> know.</i>

13:40.657 --> 13:43.457
<i>I read it in a book by al-Biruni long ago.</i>

13:46.017 --> 13:50.347
"He created the sun, moon, and stars
 to be subservient to His command."

13:50.897 --> 13:52.787
So it is written in the Quran.

13:53.547 --> 13:59.147
That is to say, the movement of the stars 
is a blessing granted to us by Allah.

